WEBVTT

00:01:26.956 --> 00:01:30.156
At the same time, solar energy,
electric vehicles,

00:01:30.196 --> 00:01:32.316
were just starting to come into their own,

00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:35.956
and it was actually cheaper
to use these than burn oil.

00:01:35.956 --> 00:01:38.556
So Hawaii presented
this perfect opportunity

00:01:38.596 --> 00:01:41.516
to demonstrate how to transition
an entire economy

00:01:41.556 --> 00:01:42.876
off of fossil fuels.

00:01:43.356 --> 00:01:44.876
It was all getting real.

00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:47.676
The battery that we’d written
a check for, in DC,

00:01:47.716 --> 00:01:49.996
was now on a ship on its way to Hawaii,

00:01:50.036 --> 00:01:52.836
ready to be installed
just a few miles from my home.

00:01:53.836 --> 00:01:56.996
And so Maurice and I,
seeing this transition was happening,

00:01:56.996 --> 00:01:59.636
and the fact that we needed
many new technologies

00:01:59.636 --> 00:02:00.956
in order to make it work,